## What I annotated

**App:** "CuratedPicks", a Vite/React/shadcn product-recommendation site (the real cwd was `data/WebTestBench/web_applications_hinted/WebTestBench_0001`, not the repo root).

All 6 screens: **home**, **products**, **product detail**, **category**, **admin**, **404** — plus the shared `Header` (incl. mobile drawer), `Footer`, `ProductCard`, `ProductGrid`, `ProductFilters`, `CategoryBadge`, `RatingStars`. 13 files, 100 hinted elements.

## Id namespaces

`nav.*` / `search.*` / `footer.*` (shared chrome) · `home.hero|featured|categories|latest.<cat>` · `products.*` · `category.*` · `product.*` · `filters.*` · `admin.form.*` / `admin.products.*` · `error.*`

## Collections — all 13 fold

The key trap was `ProductCard`, rendered in **8** different collections. On the home page Sony/Peloton/Dyson each appear **twice** (featured *and* their category row), so per §8 I threaded a `collectionId` into `ProductCard`/`ProductGrid` and made it **required** — TypeScript now makes a half-formed item id impossible. Same for the desktop/mobile nav and search (`search.query` vs `search.query.mobile`, identical `state`), which genuinely coexist in the DOM when the drawer is open.

Per §3 I extracted the sort/rating/category option lists into arrays used *both* to render the menu and to build `data-semtag-options`, so trigger and menu can't drift.

## Verification

- **Validator:** 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 info.
- **Project checks:** `tsc` clean, build clean, lint **identical to baseline** (3 pre-existing errors in `tailwind.config.ts`, `ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx` — those were already failing, I didn't touch them). The CSS bundle hash is unchanged, confirming zero styling impact.
- **Runtime** (headless Chromium against the built app, since the linter can't resolve DOM ancestry): on every screen ids are unique page-wide, every role is valid — **nothing lands in `other`** — and every `.item.` id resolves to a real collection ancestor. Verified folding counts (e.g. `admin.products` 57, `products.grid` 45), the mobile-drawer-open state, and that search/sort/navigation still behave correctly through semtag selectors.

## Deliberate gaps

- **Admin specs editor** — the one collection I did *not* fold. Its rows are removable, so their only key is array position, which shifts on delete. §7 forbids index keys, so I made it a `region` with an `admin.form.specs.add` action rather than smuggle an index past the linter. The row inputs stay unhinted (still reachable via their placeholders).
- **Unhinted by design:** decorative icons, layout wrappers, the card image link (duplicates the adjacent title link), and section headings. `product.review` is a `region` not an `observable` — that keeps a ~500-char review body out of every snapshot.
- **Residual risk:** ids key off `product.slug` and slugified spec labels. If an admin creates two products with the same name, or one product with two identically-labelled specs, those ids would collide — that's a pre-existing data-model ambiguity in the app, not something the hints introduce.

